      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-prot">Protracted path:</strong> Post-MOU diplomatic track maintains form without substance — F8 produces a public statement but no substantive demilitarisation progress, Hormuz remains below 50 transits/day (F9, 81% NO-path), and Israel's election cycle (F7, 87% YES-path) locks its government into caretaker status through Oct 27.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-desc">De-escalation path:</strong> F8 YES (60%) produces a joint framework communiqué triggering incremental Hormuz fee suspension and demining acceleration, with F12 YES (25%) enabling an Iranian decision-making signal that clears the governance-uncertainty discount and allows a reciprocal Israeli drawdown from Lebanon forward positions.</p>
    </div>
